.TH PROGRAM_FLASH_ALL_FPGA_AL9.SH 1 "2026-10-06" "otsdaq-mu2e 11.03.00" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
program_flash_all_FPGA_AL9.sh \- write one MCS image to the BPI configuration
flash of every JTAG-attached FPGA on this node, boot from it, then reset PCIe
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B program_flash_all_FPGA_AL9.sh
.RB [ NORESET ]
.RB [ NOKILL ]
.I mcsfile
.RI [ dryrun ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B program_flash_all_FPGA_AL9.sh
changes the image that each FPGA loads at power-up.
.BR program_all_FPGA_AL9.sh (1)
only changes the running, volatile configuration.
The argument handling, the USB JTAG scan and the final PCIe reset are the
same in both scripts.
The difference is the per-target command.
For the
.IR N th
adapter (USB
.B 0403:6014
FTDI,
.B 03fd:0013
or
.B 03fd:0008
Xilinx, in sysfs order) it runs:
.PP
.EX
/home/mu2ehwdev/program_flash_one_FPGA_AL9.sh N mcsfile mt28gu01gaax1e\-bpi\-x16
.EE
.PP
The flash part is hard-coded.
DTCs fitted with the older
.B mt28gu512aax1e\-bpi\-x16
part need
.I program_flash_one_FPGA_AL9.sh
to be run by hand with that part as its third argument.
The source comment beside the call reads "does not work t try both flash
types!".
.PP
.I program_flash_one_FPGA_AL9.sh
sources the Vivado Lab 2021.2 environment and appends a line to
.IR /home/mu2ehwdev/.Xil/vivado_user_log.txt .
It then runs
.I program_flash_one_FPGA.tcl
from its own directory.
That Tcl script opens hardware target
.IR N ,
creates the configuration-memory object for device 0, and erases, programs
and verifies the flash (blank check and checksum are off).
It then issues
.BR boot_hw_device ,
so the FPGA reconfigures from the new flash image immediately.
Unlike
.IR program_one_FPGA_AL9.sh ,
it does not take
.IR /tmp/mu2e.lock ,
and it has no
.B #!
line.
.PP
Unless
.B NORESET
is given, the script then runs
.B sudo
.IB dir /reset_PCIe_AL9.sh
(with
.B NOKILL
if given).
This kills every
.B xdaq.exe
and
.B boardreader
on the node; see
.BR reset_PCIe_AL9.sh (1).
There is no confirmation prompt.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B NORESET
Must be the first argument.
Skips the PCIe reset.
The FPGAs have already rebooted from flash, so the
.B mu2e
driver is left bound to a device that has been reconfigured underneath it.
A later reset is needed.
.TP
.B NOKILL
Must be the first argument, or the second after
.BR NORESET .
It is passed to
.BR reset_PCIe_AL9.sh (1).
.TP
.I mcsfile
The flash image
.RI ( .mcs ).
The existence check runs relative to the caller's working directory.
.I program_flash_one_FPGA_AL9.sh
does not change directory, so a relative path also works.
.TP
.I dryrun
Any non-empty second positional argument.
The program and reset commands are printed, not run.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /home/mu2ehwdev/program_flash_one_FPGA_AL9.sh
Per-target flash programmer, called by absolute path.
.TP
.I /home/xilinx/Vivado_Lab/2021.2/settings64.sh
Vivado Lab environment.
.TP
.I /home/mu2ehwdev/.Xil/vivado_user_log.txt
Append-only record of each flash write.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
No variable changes the script's behaviour.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 1
.I mcsfile
is non-empty and is not an existing file.
.TP
.B 0
Every other case, including a Vivado erase, program or verify failure, a
wrong flash part, no JTAG adapter found, and a failed reset.
Read the Vivado output for
.B ERROR
lines, and for the
.B HIGH
line that the per-target script flags.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
/home/mu2ehwdev/program_flash_all_FPGA_AL9.sh \e
    /home/mu2ehwdev/DTC_Firmware/<version>/DTC.mcs
.EE
.PP
Older flash part, one target, by hand:
.PP
.EX
/home/mu2ehwdev/program_flash_one_FPGA_AL9.sh 0 /abs/path/DTC.mcs \e
    mt28gu512aax1e\-bpi\-x16
.EE
.SH CAVEATS
As in
.BR program_all_FPGA_AL9.sh (1),
running the script with no
.I mcsfile
does not print usage.
The unquoted
.B [ ! \-f $MCSFILE ]
test passes, the per-target script is called with too few arguments and
does nothing, and the PCIe reset still runs and kills processes.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR program_all_FPGA_AL9.sh (1),
.BR boot_from_flash_all_DTCs_AL9.sh (1),
.BR reset_PCIe_AL9.sh (1),
.BR check_firmware_version.sh (1),
.BR otsdaq-mu2e-tools (7)
